meta {
  name: Prod env guard
  seq: 90
}

docs {
  > Verifies the Configure PROD guard rules on the Workspace API:
  > - Creating Configure resources is blocked when `X-Env-Type` is `Prod`.
  > - Editing a persisted PROD Configure resource requires the OM role (403 otherwise).
  > - Child writes/deletes under a persisted PROD parent are blocked even when the
  >   request spoofs a DEV header (message contains `published (PROD)`).
  > - Sharing/removing access to a persisted PROD Configure resource is allowed
  >   for a user with share rights (see `resource-user-access/prod-share`).
  > - Assigning agents to a PROD queue requires the OM role.
  >
  > Work-item inserts are intentionally NOT blocked in PROD: work items are runtime
  > data, not Configure resources (see `create-workitem-prod-not-blocked`). The
  > Configure UI still disables interactive uploads via `ActionLock`.
  >
  > Prerequisites (like the other Configure requests):
  > - A valid session/token setup and selected tenant/space.
  > - `SKILL_ID` / `QUEUE_ID` seeded by running their insert requests first in Dev,
  >   for the sub-resource cases.
  > - To run the delete case, set `PROD_QUEUE_ID` (Global Environment) to an existing
  >   PROD queue id.
  > - Update/assign/share cases require `PROD_OM_ACCESS_TOKEN`, `PROD_TD_ACCESS_TOKEN`,
  >   `PROD_OM_QUEUE_ID`, `PROD_TD_QUEUE_ID`, `DEV_TD_QUEUE_ID` and `PROD_TD_SHAREE_ID`
  >   (a tenant user who is not the queue owner) in the Global Environment. The OM-owned
  >   PROD queue and TD-owned DEV queue must be dedicated authorization fixtures matching
  >   the payloads in the requests.
  > - Nested-resource spoof/delete cases require `PROD_KB_ID`, `PROD_SKILL_ID`,
  >   and `PROD_SKILL_FILE_ID` pointing to existing PROD parents/files.
}
